1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:06,610
When we were finally dismissed from the last class of the day, the students streamed out of the classrooms.
当天最后一节课终于下课了，学生们从各个教室蜂拥而出。

2
00:00:07,410 --> 00:00:09,410
It was another boring day after school.
放学后，又是无聊的一天。

3
00:00:10,210 --> 00:00:12,050
I dragged my feet home as I sighed.
我叹着气，拖着脚步往家走。

4
00:00:12,850 --> 00:00:15,510
Yet another uneventful day, I thought.
又是平淡无奇的一天，我想。

5
00:00:16,310 --> 00:00:19,240
Little did I know that the day would take a turn for the worse.
我万万没想到，这一天的情况会急转直下。

6
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:22,480
The lift lobby of my flat was old and dirty.
我住的那栋公寓楼的电梯间又旧又脏。

7
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:27,540
The walls, which were painted white, had been dirtied over many years.
墙壁原本刷成白色，多年下来早已脏兮兮的。

8
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:31,440
I reached my flat’s lobby, pressed the lift button and went in.
我走到公寓楼的电梯间，按了电梯按钮，走了进去。

9
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:36,690
Just then, Mrs Lim, my elderly neighbour, hobbled in.
就在这时，我的邻居、年迈的林太太蹒跚着走了进来。

10
00:00:37,490 --> 00:00:41,900
She looked ancient with tissue-paper-white hair, wearing a faded old-fashioned dress.
她头发像薄纸一样白，穿着一条褪了色的老式连衣裙，看上去非常苍老。

11
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:47,490
I held the lift door open, flashing a friendly smile, and politely greeted her.
我扶住电梯门，露出友善的微笑，礼貌地向她问好。

12
00:00:48,290 --> 00:00:51,180
I asked her how she felt that day and pressed the buttons.
我问她那天身体怎么样，然后按了楼层按钮。

13
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:56,060
She thanked me for being so polite, then we were silent for the rest of the ride.
她谢谢我这么有礼貌，之后一路上我们都没再说话。

14
00:00:56,860 --> 00:00:58,920
The lift went down faster and faster.
电梯越降越快。

15
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:03,810
There were loud clanking sounds here and there while the lift grew slower and slower.
电梯里四处传来响亮的哐当声，而电梯却越来越慢。

16
00:01:04,610 --> 00:01:08,880
My heart beat hard and fast as my hands turned cold and wet with sweat.
我的心怦怦狂跳，双手变得冰凉，满是冷汗。

17
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:13,310
Unfortunately, the lift came to an abrupt stop at the fifth floor.
不幸的是，电梯在五楼突然停了下来。

18
00:01:14,110 --> 00:01:17,720
I pressed the buttons hard several times, but it was of no help.
我用力按了好几次按钮，却一点用也没有。

19
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:20,260
The lights on the buttons had gone out.
按钮上的灯都已经熄灭了。

20
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:22,990
It soon dawned on me that we were trapped.
我很快明白过来：我们被困住了。

21
00:01:23,790 --> 00:01:25,690
An icy fear crept up my spine.
一股冰冷的恐惧顺着我的脊背爬了上来。

22
00:01:26,490 --> 00:01:28,080
Mrs Lim was hysterical.
林太太歇斯底里起来。

23
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:31,580
“We will never get out!” she cried with her face pale.
“我们再也出不去了！”她脸色苍白，大声哭喊着。

24
00:01:32,380 --> 00:01:34,080
It had become a colourless mask.
那张脸已经变成了一张毫无血色的面具。

25
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:36,260
I had no time to lose.
我一刻也不能耽误了。

26
00:01:37,060 --> 00:01:38,960
I pressed the bell in the lift immediately.
我立刻按下了电梯里的警铃。

27
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:43,160
The sound was surely deafening, but what other choice did I have?
那声音想必震耳欲聋，可我还能有什么别的办法呢？

28
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:45,800
Mrs Lim burst into tears.
林太太突然放声大哭。

29
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:53,700
I tried my very best to comfort her, telling her that everything would be all right and that we needed to find out how to get out safely.
我尽全力安慰她，告诉她一切都会好起来的，我们得想办法安全地出去。

30
00:01:54,500 --> 00:02:00,270
Mrs Lim began having trouble breathing, and I immediately helped her sit down and loosened her collar.
林太太开始呼吸困难，我立刻扶她坐下，松开了她的衣领。

31
00:02:01,070 --> 00:02:03,680
Several minutes passed, but no help came.
几分钟过去了，却没有人来救援。

32
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:05,090
Bang!
砰！

33
00:02:05,890 --> 00:02:10,270
My hopes were lifted when I heard the firefighters on the other side of the lift door.
听到电梯门另一侧传来消防员的声音，我又燃起了希望。
